(subclass Fork Device)

(documentation Fork EnglishLanguage "An implement with two or more
pointed prongs attached to a handle, used especially for taking up food,
for pitching material such as hay or straw, and for digging. A Fork is a
Device, i.e. an artifact whose purpose is to serve as an instrument in
some process. Every Fork has at least two distinct Prongs as physical
parts, and typical forks function as instruments in the processes of
Eating, Digging, or Throwing (e.g. pitching hay).")

(termFormat EnglishLanguage Fork "fork")

(subclass Prong Object)

(documentation Prong EnglishLanguage "A pointed, projecting part of an
implement, such as one of the tines of a Fork. A Prong is a physical
Object that is part of an implement and serves to pierce, lift, or hold
material.")

(=>
  (instance ?F Fork)
  (exists (?P1 ?P2)
    (and
      (instance ?P1 Prong)
      (instance ?P2 Prong)
      (not (equal ?P1 ?P2))
      (part ?P1 ?F)
      (part ?P2 ?F))))

(=>
  (instance ?F Fork)
  (or
    (exists (?E)
      (and (instance ?E Eating) (instrument ?E ?F)))
    (exists (?D)
      (and (instance ?D Digging) (instrument ?D ?F)))
    (exists (?T)
      (and (instance ?T Throwing) (instrument ?T ?F)))))